308
00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:32.397
The decisions.

309
00:21:32.397 --> 00:21:35.848
Who owns each namespace,
the Grid or a cloud.

310
00:21:35.848 --> 00:21:40.148
Which middleware platform, and so which
network and resolver path it uses.

311
00:21:40.148 --> 00:21:42.110
The hub design in each cloud.

312
00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:45.524
And whether Oracle's private
access is needed at all,

313
00:21:45.524 --> 00:21:47.985
remembering that it's routing, not DNS.

314
00:21:47.985 --> 00:21:50.460
The next steps are the
things I couldn't verify.

315
00:21:50.460 --> 00:21:56.285
Which Oracle environment and hostnames
the agency's Core HCM tenant will use.

316
00:21:56.285 --> 00:22:00.296
Whether API-driven inbound
provisioning is available in the U.S.

317
00:22:00.296 --> 00:22:01.810
Government Graph cloud.

318
00:22:01.810 --> 00:22:05.951
Whether Azure's DNS Private
Resolver, Lifecycle Workflows and

319
00:22:05.951 --> 00:22:10.410
Connect private endpoints are
available in the government clouds.

320
00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:13.777
And the VMware install
guides' DNS rules and Oracle's

321
00:22:13.777 --> 00:22:16.910
own connectivity patterns,
which I couldn't open.

322
00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:18.585
They're all listed in the backup.

323
00:22:18.585 --> 00:22:19.722
Where does this fit?

324
00:22:19.722 --> 00:22:22.750
Book 03 covers HR-driven identity,

325
00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:29.561
with Federal HR 2.0 in Chapter 03 and
the provisioning pipeline in Chapter 05.

326
00:22:29.561 --> 00:22:36.197
Book 08 covers DNS, DHCP and IP address
management: split-brain DNS in Chapter 02,

327
00:22:36.197 --> 00:22:43.038
cloud private endpoints in Chapter 07,
the reference architecture in Chapter 08,

328
00:22:43.038 --> 00:22:46.510
and the migration sequence in Chapter 10.

329
00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:52.849
